{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@property","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"nonatomic","kind":"keyword"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"readonly","kind":"keyword"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NSArray<MLNPolygon *>","preciseIdentifier":"c:Q$objc(cs)NSArray","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" * ","kind":"text"},{"text":"interiorPolygons","kind":"identifier"},{"text":";","kind":"text"}],"languages":["occ"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The area occupied by any interior polygons is excluded from the overall shape.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Interior polygons should not overlap. An interior polygon should not have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interior polygons of its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If there are no interior polygons, the value of this property is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon\/interiorpolygons"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The array of polygons nested inside the receiver.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"externalID":"c:objc(cs)MLNPolygon(py)interiorPolygons","symbolKind":"property","title":"interiorPolygons","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"interiorPolygons"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"interiorPolygons"}],"role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"occ","url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon\/interiorPolygons"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"]]},"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolygon/interiorPolygons":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon\/interiorpolygons","title":"interiorPolygons","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The array of polygons nested inside the receiver."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"interiorPolygons"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon\/interiorPolygons"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre":{"title":"MapLibre","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Powerful, free and open-source mapping toolkit with full control over data sources and styling."}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolygon":{"fragments":[{"text":"MLNPolygon","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MLNPolygon","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"},{"type":"text","text":" object represents a closed shape consisting of four or more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, specified as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D"},{"type":"text","text":" instances, and the edges that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connect them. For example, you could use a polygon shape to represent a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"building, a lake, or an area you want to highlight."}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}